    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d558">

                <pb facs="0577" n="411" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg411"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.00/1376</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Gonzales to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-03T22:00:00-05:29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 3, 1917, 10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your June 2, 4 p.m. Having expressed himself as reported in my May 16, 11 p.m.
                    replying to Department’s offer May 15, 3 p.m. President said nothing to
                    announcement in Department’s May 18, 4 p.m. that troops would be sent to
                    Guantanamo station except to repeat there would be no occasion call upon their
                    services. He expected to relieve with regular troops all marines then guarding
                    property. Conditions have improved daily since inauguration of the President and
                    nothing to indicate Government needs assistance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
